# Trigger UI verifier demo

When work touches **user-visible behavior** or qualifies as a **large change**, the implementing agent must run functional BDD verification **before** marking the task complete or opening a review-ready PR.

## Delegate

Foreground **`/ui-verifier-demo`** (or Task → `ui-verifier-demo` subagent). The verifier is **readonly** — it reports only.

Follow [obsidian-ui-verifier-demo](../../skills/obsidian-ui-verifier-demo/SKILL.md).

## When required

Any of:

- New or changed user flow (commands, modals, settings, status, errors, permissions)
- **Large change heuristic:** ≥3 non-test files under `src/ui/`, `src/hooks/`, plugin settings tab, or `styles.css`
- Same bar as [pr-product-demos](./pr-product-demos.mdc) (complex / user-facing PR)

## Parent obligations

1. Deploy + reload + identity gate **before** delegating. Run [obsidian-ui-visibility](../../skills/obsidian-ui-visibility/SKILL.md) before screenshots or recordings.
2. Pass plugin id, behavior summary, and repo-specific verify hints in the subagent prompt.
3. Block **done** on verifier **FAIL** (any P0 scenario or deploy gate).
4. On **PARTIAL**, fix P1 failures or document accepted gaps in PR/chat.
5. Attach `ui-verifier-demo-report.md` and evidence paths to PR when applicable.

## Skip (narrow)

Docs/comments only, user `/no-test`, or zero behavior impact — one smoke `eval` still recommended on cloud.

## Failures

The verifier must explain each failure with **Expected behavior**, **Observed behavior**, and **BDD gap** (how observation violates the story). Parent summarizes verdict in the final message.
